{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Living the Dream"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Big Upps!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le16ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are four different future tenses that talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Will: </span><ul><li>When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future.</li></ul>For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I will call you later</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Be going to: </span><ul><li>When you ask about intentions</li></ul> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Are you going to go to the meeting later?</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous: </span><ul><li> When you talk about things that are arranged, on the  agenda or booked for the future.</li></ul> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">The meeting is happening at 9 a.m. sharp tomorrow. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Simple Present: </span><ul><li>When you talk about schedules </li></ul>For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"> The presentation starts at 3.30.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am running errands today."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's on tonight at five."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I am going to work really hard. I promise."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will definitely be better than this woman."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking Hypothetically About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would have</span>, <span class=\"strong\">should have</span> and <span class=\"strong\">could have </span>can be used to talk about hypothetical situations in the past that may or may not be true."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Could have</span> (+ past participle)</span></br><span class=\"strong\">Could have</span> is used to talk about something that was possible in the past and you had the ability to do something in the past, but you didn't do it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could have gotten that job</span>, if I applied earlier.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You also use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span> to make a guess about something that happened in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Why is Mark not here yet?</span></br><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">could have been</span> stuck in traffic or he <span class=\"strong\">could have overslept</span></span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Should have </span>(+ past participle)</span></br> <span class=\"strong\">Should have</span> is used for giving advice for past events. We often use it to display regret when we think something was a good idea in the past, but we didn't do it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">should have applied</span> sooner</span>. <br/>(I regret not applying sooner)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't have answered</span> that question like that.</span></br> (You should have answered that question in another way)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Would have </span>( + past participle)</span></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Would have</span> is used to talk about something you wanted to do but you didn't do. This is very similar to the third conditional, but we don't need an 'if clause'."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">would have called </span>you, but I didn't know your number. </span><br/>(I wanted to call you but I didn't know your number, so I didn't call you.)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She shouldn't have said that, it comes off as being informal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She should have answered more formally. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She could have said, \u201cFine thank you. And you?\u201d "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I would have been perfect for this job."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wouldn't have said that."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to ramble on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to talk without stopping"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The interviewer is trying to make small talk and she's just rambling on."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when listening to an interview."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to start off on the wrong foot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to begin in an awkward or unpleasant way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  This interview has started off on the wrong foot. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "formally"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a formal way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  She should have answered more formally. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "professionalism"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an attitude appropriate for the workplace"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She should have answered in a way that demonstrated her professionalism. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "positively"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a good way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Her answer reflected positively on her overall character. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about a job interview."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain what I regretted."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain what I would have changed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I reflect on my experience and talk about what I will do next time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my story clearly and concisely."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a story about your worst job interview experience."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you don't have one, make one up."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Be very detailed in your description."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What would you have done differently and what you will do next time?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use passive modals to explain what you would have changed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Get into groups and compare stories."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Vote on the best one."}]}], "labs": [{"exerc